From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Deep sleeping apps, with Put unused apps to sleep

Mobile Manager > App blocker becomes Deep sleeping apps (owner decision
2026-11-06, after the deep sleep of recent Samsung phones): the same
switch per launcher app, Android's Restricted background mode plus a
stop, now named for what it does. A new switch at the top, Put unused
apps to sleep (off by default), schedules a daily pass while the phone
is idle that puts every launcher app not opened, installed or updated
for 3 days into deep sleep. Sable's own apps, the apps 1208 never lists
(home, dialer, SMS, keyboard, Settings), enabled accessibility services
and notification listeners, device admins and the live wallpaper are
left alone, and an app the user wakes on the page stays awake. Its row
says it was put to sleep for not being opened.

Pure DeepSleepPolicy with host tests in tests/sable-apps.
